  "notes": "{蹴|け}る means to kick or to reject (figuratively).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ボールを{蹴|け}る: to kick a ball\n- {足|あし}で{蹴|け}る: to kick with one's foot\n- {強|つよ}く{蹴|け}る: to kick hard\n\nCOMPOUND VERBS:\n- {蹴|け}り{飛|と}ばす: to kick away/off\n- {蹴|け}り{上|あ}げる: to kick upward\n- {蹴|け}り{倒|たお}す: to kick down\n\nFIGURATIVE USES:\n- {申|もう}し{出|で}を{蹴|け}る: to reject an offer\n- {誘|さそ}いを{蹴|け}る: to turn down an invitation\n- チャンスを{蹴|け}る: to pass up a chance\n\nSPORTS:\n- サッカーでボールを{蹴|け}る: to kick the ball in soccer\n- {蹴|け}り{技|わざ}: kicking technique (martial arts)",
